    "result_text": "The test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`), and the audit log confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` (region) + `27` (FY, since a 2026-09 registration falls in the fiscal year ending 2027) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `1` (Luhn CHK).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe internal `Owner.customerCode` field now stores the unified `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`); the DTO exposes only `memberId`. Four files touched, each edit small and confined to a low-complexity method:\n\n1. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the identity-assigning step now builds `core = REGION + FY + HASH8` and stores `core + CheckDigit.of(core)`. The region-selection logic (the high-complexity part) is untouched; I changed one statement into two. Collision handling in `DeduplicateCustomerCode` needed **no change** \u2014 it deduplicates whatever is stored, which is now the memberId.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings; added `memberId` (the stored value verbatim); switched the region extraction for `locality`/`timezone`/`ownerSegment` from \"substring before `-`\" to \"strip from the first digit\" (`replaceAll(\"[0-9].*\", \"\")`), which yields the leading region letters and is robust to any `-<n>` collision suffix.\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 both audit log lines (human-readable and JSON) now reference `memberId` instead of `customerCode` + `membershipNumber`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode` and `checkDigit` schema entries with a single `memberId`, and removed `membershipNumber` (the generated `OwnerDto` follows).\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n\nThe dominant cost lever is a method's surrounding-class complexity (`WMC_other`) and the number of files. So I:\n- reused the existing `CheckDigit` (Luhn) and `FiscalYear` helpers rather than adding a new class \u2014 **no new files**, keeping the file multiplier at 4;\n- left `DeduplicateCustomerCode`, `CheckDigit`, `FiscalYear`, `OwnerSegment`, `Timezone`, and the `Owner` entity **untouched**;\n- kept each edited method simple \u2014 the one high-complexity method (`AssignCustomerCode.service`, with its region if/else chain) got only a minimal 2-line change rather than absorbing the FY/check-digit assembly as new branches.",
